  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened capacity of member States to ratify and apply international labour standards and to fulfil their reporting obligations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Iraq, an ILO member since 1932, has ratified 9 of 10 fundamental Conventions (C029, C087, C098, C100, C105, C111, C138, C182, C187), 3 of 4 Governance Conventions (C081, C122, C144), and 60 Technical Conventions. In 2023, Iraq ratified Convention No. 102 on Social Security and the Maritime Labour Convention (MLC, 2006), both effective March 2024. The ILO continues to support Iraq in meeting reporting obligations.
Iraq is set to become the first country in the region to ratify Convention 190 on Violence and Harassment in the world of work based on a recent decision by the Government of Iraq  to ratify Convention 190 on Violence and Harassment in the world of work. The ILO is actively supporting the ratification process and alignment of national laws and policies. It is also assisting in reviewing Iraq&#x2019;s labour law following the ratification of Convention No. 87, with a draft amendment to be discussed in 2024 before proceeding with its referral to the Council of State.
The ILO is helping Iraq implement Convention No. 184 on Safety and Health in Agriculture, in force since May 2021, through training, policy briefs, and support for a national OSH policy for agriculture. It is also aiding in drafting a new trade union law promoting pluralism and public sector organizing, aligned with international standards and amending Labour Law No. 37.
Further, the ILO supports inclusion of Persons with Disabilities in the labour market and promotes transition to formality per Recommendation 204. It is also assisting Iraq in implementing Convention No. 94 on Labour Clauses in Public Contracts by reviewing national instructions and designing a pilot program to ensure compliance with international labour standards and Fundamental Principles and Rights at Work.</narrative>
  </description>
